Gismu (basic words) were derived from the corresponding words in a number of 
major world languages by an algorithm that took into account the number of 
speakers of the languages and some other factors.  The whole project was 
finished by a little tweaking here and there.  Cmavo are partly by tradition 
(from Loglan), partly a priori (here is a nice unused bit of word space) and 
partly from similarity to gismu of related meanings (this also had a role in 
Loglan).  Compound words are made from compound phrases by dropping bits 
(according to rules) from the components.  Words incorporating words from other 
languages are treated by Lojbanding the foreign word and attaching it to an 
explanatory Lojban predicate.  There are rules -- some rather complex -- for 
these latter two cases.





